{"c":[{"id":"9fd3bd87f83b4e2d","sum":"caret-fixture: writing AXMain makes a background window key with no activation (stage 'looked at Reference, then the form'); it ignores pid-posted Cmd-V (no Edit menu), so the host falls back to AXSelectedText, learned per app.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T133226Z-6bdfe982409203f3","text":"Writing AXMain on a background fixture window makes it the app's key window with no activation and no z-order change; use it to stage 'user looked at Reference, then went to the form'.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T133226Z-82c44796f08e654e","text":"caret-fixture ignores a pid-posted Cmd-V (no Edit menu); the host falls back to an AXSelectedText write and learns it per app (exe:caret-fixture).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c7b6f65f9bdd661f","sum":"Fill tests: grounded fill withholds nearly all (Jev 0.4-0.7) unless the source was focused just before the form, so stage a visit; caret-fixture --gold frames are view frames, AX fields are 1 pt larger each side, so match by AX frame.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T133226Z-cbf7abe12b1fb923","text":"Grounded fill withholds nearly everything (Jev confidence 0.4-0.7) unless the source window was the one focused just before the form; stage a visit first.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T133226Z-dcf0803ca75a2746","text":"Fill tests: caret-fixture's --gold frames are view frames; AX (reader and host) reports text fields 1 pt larger on every side, so match by AX frame.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
